# Session Start Protocol

## STEP 0 — READ BEFORE TOUCHING ANYTHING

1. Read `AGENTS.md` — full project context, locked decisions, current state
2. Read `TASK.md` — current sprint status
3. Read `OMEGA_PROTOCOL.md` — persona council for complex decisions
4. If working on signals/math: read `docs/SIGNAL_DEFINITIONS.md`
5. If working on frontend: read `OMEGA_UI_SWARM_PROMPT.md`

State the current focus and today's deliverable explicitly before writing code:
> "Today's session will build [X]. It touches [files]. It writes to [Supabase tables]. Tests: [pytest / npm run build]."

## CANONICAL PIPELINE ORDER — NEVER DEVIATE

Prefect Cloud runs `src/scheduler/orchestrator.py:run_daily` with this fixed sequence:
```
yields → fx_spot → cot → volatility → open_interest → macro_calendar → cross_asset
  → signals (rate, cot, vol, oi)
  → regime (classifier, composite, confidence)
  → logic (layer1_gate, layer2_directional, layer3_execution)
  → db/writer (persist)
  → validation (backtest, append-only)
  → brief (generate)
```

- Never reorder these steps
- Never suggest parallelization in pipeline modules
- New pipelines are added to the orchestrator only with explicit instruction

## PROTECTED DIRECTORIES — NEVER TOUCH

- `data/` — bulk output, never read or reference
- `briefs/` — generated briefs, never read or reference
- `runs/` — pipeline run logs, never read or reference
- `_docs/` — Obsidian vault, NEVER modify
- `_legacy_archive/` — archived material, read-only
- `.venv/` — virtual environment

## PROJECT BOUNDARIES

- Python only in pipeline. No C++. No Node.js backend.
- Next.js frontend in `web/` only. No React in pipeline.
- All persistent data goes to Supabase. Not local files in production.
- One file per signal module. Do not combine pipeline logic.
- No new dependencies without explicit approval.

## BEFORE WRITING ANY CODE

- [ ] `AGENTS.md` read and confirmed
- [ ] `TASK.md` read and confirmed
- [ ] Session deliverable stated explicitly
- [ ] No conflict with existing Supabase schema
- [ ] No existing script does what you are about to build
- [ ] `cd pipeline && pytest` passes before changes (baseline)
